mingw: do not force -lstdc++ in a static build.

Under JPEGXL_STATIC libjxl feeds every target
`-Wl,-Bstatic -lstdc++ -lpthread -Wl,-Bdynamic`. The block keeps a static
libstdc++ apart from a dynamic pthread; the engine links libc++, which has
no libstdc++ to find ("unable to find library -lstdc++") and no such tie.
-lpthread stays: jxl_threads asks for a bare -lpthread.

--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -280,7 +280,7 @@
     # object files and therefore discarded. This should be set in the
     # INTERFACE_LINK_LIBRARIES of Threads::Threads but some third_part targets
     # don't depend on it.
-    link_libraries(-Wl,-Bstatic -lstdc++ -lpthread -Wl,-Bdynamic)
+    link_libraries(-Wl,-Bstatic -lpthread -Wl,-Bdynamic)
   elseif(CMAKE_USE_PTHREADS_INIT)
     # "whole-archive" is not supported on OSX.
     if (NOT APPLE)
